# Styling Guidelines

## Tailwind CSS

This project uses **Tailwind CSS 4** with CSS variables for theming.

### Global Styles

Global styles and CSS variables are defined in [src/styles/globals.css](mdc:src/styles/globals.css).

### CSS Variables

Theme colors use CSS variables in HSL format:

- `--background`, `--foreground`
- `--primary`, `--primary-foreground`
- `--secondary`, `--secondary-foreground`
- `--accent`, `--accent-foreground`
- `--destructive`, `--destructive-foreground`
- `--muted`, `--muted-foreground`
- `--card`, `--card-foreground`
- `--border`, `--input`, `--ring`

Access these via Tailwind utilities:

```tsx
<div className="bg-background text-foreground">
  <Button className="bg-primary text-primary-foreground">Primary Button</Button>
</div>
```

## Utility Function

Use the `cn()` utility from [src/lib/utils.ts](mdc:src/lib/utils.ts) for conditional classes:

```typescript
import { cn } from "~/lib/utils";

<div className={cn(
  "base-classes",
  isActive && "active-classes",
  variant === "large" && "large-classes"
)} />
```

## Best Practices

### Responsive Design

Use Tailwind's responsive prefixes:

```tsx
<div className="flex flex-col md:flex-row lg:gap-8">
  {/* Mobile: column, Desktop: row */}
</div>
```

### Common Patterns

**Container with padding:**

```tsx
<div className="container mx-auto px-4 py-8">
```

**Centered content:**

```tsx
<div className="flex min-h-screen items-center justify-center">
```

**Card with hover:**

```tsx
<div className="rounded-lg border bg-card p-4 transition-colors hover:bg-accent">
```

**Truncated text:**

```tsx
<p className="truncate">Long text here...</p>
<p className="line-clamp-3">Multi-line truncation...</p>
```

### Avoid

- ❌ Inline styles - use Tailwind classes instead
- ❌ Arbitrary values without reason - prefer design tokens
- ❌ Deep nesting of conditional classes - extract to variants
- ❌ Modifying `globals.css` without considering theme implications

### Animation

Use Tailwind's built-in animations:

```tsx
<div className="animate-spin">Loading...</div>
<div className="transition-all duration-300 ease-in-out">
```

For custom animations, use `tw-animate-css` package when needed.

## Dark Mode

The project supports dark mode via CSS variables. Both light and dark mode variables are defined in [src/styles/globals.css](mdc:src/styles/globals.css).

Use the `dark:` prefix for dark mode specific styles if needed:

```tsx
<div className="bg-white dark:bg-gray-900">
```

## Component Styling Priority

1. Use shadcn component variants when available
2. Add Tailwind utilities via `className` prop
3. Use `cn()` for conditional styling
4. Create wrapper components for complex patterns
5. Only add to globals.css for truly global styles
